SUMMARY:Milky Way · Bogey Hole · Core over the convict cut ocean pool
LOCATION:The Bogey Hole\, below King Edward Park\, York Drive\, Newcastle N
 SW 2300
GEO:-32.93522;151.78164
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-32.93522,151.78164
DESCRIPTION:WHAT: The core rising over the Tasman Sea above the Bogey Hole\
 , the ocean pool cut into the rock platform by convicts in about 1820. Pai
 rs with the Caves Beach sea caves the next night.\nPriority: Optional\n\nW
 HEN (Sydney time)\nNight of Fri 02 Apr into Sat 03 Apr 2027.\nShoot window
 : 23:19 to 01:59 (core between 8° and 60° high\, sky fully dark\, moon d
 own\, low tide).\nRock platform shoot: the window is cut to low tide plus 
 or minus 90 minutes.\nBest composition: about 01:14\, core 30° high in th
 e ESE.\nArrive by 22:34 to set up and focus.\nSunset 18:47 · astronomical
  dusk 20:09 · astronomical dawn 05:43 · sunrise 07:05\nMoon: new moon We
 d 07 Apr 09:51. 19% lit and below the horizon during the window. Moonrise 
 Sat 03:13 · Moonset Fri 16:09\n\nCORE POSITION\n23:30  altitude 10°\, az
 imuth 118° ESE\n00:00  altitude 16°\, azimuth 115° ESE\n00:30  altitude
  22°\, azimuth 111° ESE\n01:00  altitude 28°\, azimuth 108° ESE\n01:30
   altitude 34°\, azimuth 105° ESE\n02:00  altitude 40°\, azimuth 102° 
 ESE\n\nTIDES (BOM prediction\, Newcastle)\nNewcastle is the nearest BOM st
 andard port. Treat times as approximate for this site.\nThe window above i
 s cut to low tide 00:30 (0.80 m) plus or minus 90 minutes.\nLow water Sat 
 00:30  0.80 m\nAt the best composition (01:14): about 0.83 m and rising.\n
 Predictions exclude swell\, wind setup and wave run up. Check BOM coastal 
 waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nSource table: https://www.bom.gov.
 au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP004.pdf\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nThe Bogey 
 Hole\, below King Edward Park\, York Drive\, Newcastle NSW 2300\nCamera pi
 n: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-32.93522\,151.78164\nF
 ace ESE (azimuth 107°) at 01:14.\nStraight line from Neutral Bay: about 1
 13 km.\n\nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\nFE 12-24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to
  14 mm for single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II for a sharper multi row panor
 ama.\n12 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm: up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 
 9 s. 35 mm f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForeground: separate longer frame
 s at ISO 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from the same tripod position.\
 nPeak Design travel tripod\, red head torch\, dew heater strap on the lens
 .\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Access: steps lead down from King Edward Park to the p
 ool platform. Park on York Drive or at the top of The Terrace and walk dow
 n through the park.\n- Official listing: free entry. Not suitable for peop
 le with access needs.\n- Waves break over the pool in any real swell\, and
  people have been washed off these rocks. Shoot from the steps or the clif
 f top if sets reach the platform.\n- Open ocean to the ESE. Newcastle city
  glow sits behind you to the west.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camer
 a pin\, subject pin and time set): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-32.
 93522\,151.78164&center=-32.93522\,151.78164&z=15&dt=2027-04-02T14%3A14%3A
 00.000Z\nPhotoPills: Planner > drop the pin at the camera coordinates > se
 t the date and time above > Milky Way layer. Use Night AR on site to confi
 rm the core path.\nCheck cloud (BOM and Windy) and light pollution (lightp
 ollutionmap.info) two days out.\n\nSOURCES\nMoon phases: US Naval Observat
 ory 2027 table (aa.usno.navy.mil).\nSun\, moon and core positions: compute
 d with Skyfield and JPL DE421 for the camera pin.\nCoordinates: OpenStreet
 Map. Terrain horizons: SRTM 30 m via OpenTopoData.\nTide predictions: Bure
 au of Meteorology 2027 tide tables\, Copyright Commonwealth of Australia 2
 026. Based on Bureau of Meteorology information that has been modified. Th
 e Bureau does not necessarily support or endorse\, or have any connection 
 with\, this product\, and gives no warranty about the information. Full te
 rms: page 4 of the source PDF.
