 d wave run up. Check BOM coastal waters and swell forecasts on the day.\nS
 ource table: https://www.bom.gov.au/ntc/IDO59001/IDO59001_2027_NSW_TP006.p
 df\n\nCAMERA POSITION\nBombo Headland Quarry Geological Site viewpoint\, C
 ommissioners Lane\, Bombo NSW 2533\nCamera pin: https://www.google.com/map
 s/search/?api=1&query=-34.65005\,150.86242\nSubject pin (Bombo basalt colu
 mns): https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=-34.65037\,150.86344
 \nBombo basalt columns is 100 m away on bearing 111° (ESE). At 23:43 the 
 core is 5 degrees left of it\, 30° up. To stack the core straight above i
 t\, move about 8 m to your right\, keeping the same distance.\nStraight li
 ne from Neutral Bay: about 96 km.\n\nKIT AND STARTING SETTINGS (Sony A1)\n
 FE 12-24mm F2.8 GM at 12 to 14 mm for single frames. FE 35mm F1.4 GM II fo
 r a sharper multi row panorama.\n12 mm f/2.8: ISO 3200\, up to 19 s. 14 mm
 : up to 16 s. 24 mm: up to 9 s. 35 mm f/1.4: up to 5 s (NPF rule).\nForegr
 ound: separate longer frames at ISO 800 to 1600\, or blue hour frames from
  the same tripod position.\nPeak Design travel tripod\, red head torch\, d
 ew heater strap on the lens.\n\nFIELD NOTES\n- Confirm current track and c
 ar park access with Kiama Council before the trip.\n- Old quarry: loose ro
 ck and drop offs. Scout in daylight and keep to marked paths.\n- The colum
 ns can block the lowest part of the core. Shoot from the upper terrace.\n-
  A low level light panel on the columns from the side adds texture. Keep i
 t dim.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE YOU GO\nTPE Web (camera pin\, subject pin and time
  set): https://app.photoephemeris.com/?ll=-34.65005\,150.86242&center=-34.
 65005\,150.86242&z=15&dt=2027-04-10T13%3A43%3A00.000Z&sll=-34.65037\,150.8
